 # Run review queue fixture
 
-TODO: document the completed feature, API behavior, and operating limits.
+This dependency-free fixture records one current review per benchmark run and
+renders the queue as server-generated HTML. Saving the same `runId` updates its
+review while preserving the original creation timestamp.
+
+## API routes
+
+- `POST /api/reviews` creates or updates a review. It returns `201` for a new
+  run and `200` for an update.
+- `GET /api/reviews` returns all reviews plus an unfiltered summary. Add
+  `?decision=approve`, `?decision=reject`, or `?decision=needs-work` to filter
+  the returned review list without changing the summary.
+- `GET /api/reviews/:runId` returns one review, or `review_not_found` with
+  status `404` when no review exists for that run.
+
+POST bodies accept only the string fields `runId`, `decision`, `reviewer`, and
+`note`. Values are trimmed. Run IDs use the form `run-...`; decisions are
+`approve`, `reject`, or `needs-work`; reviewer names contain 2–40 characters;
+and notes contain at most 240 characters. A note is required for rejection and
+needs-work decisions but may be empty for approval.
+
+Invalid input returns status `400` with `validation_failed` and a `fields`
+object containing all detected problems. Unknown body fields are reported in
+sorted order and invalid data is not saved. Malformed requests return
+`invalid_request`; unsupported methods on known routes return
+`method_not_allowed` with an `allow` header; and unknown routes return
+`not_found`. All responses use JSON-style bodies and declare JSON UTF-8 content.
+
+## Operating limit
+
+The store is in memory and is not durable. All reviews reset whenever the
+process restarts; use persistent storage before relying on this fixture for
+production records.
+
+Run the complete fixture tests with:
+
+```sh
+node --test review-queue.test.mjs student-tests.mjs
+```
